.TH GIT-NANNY 1 "2026-08-13" "git-nanny" "Git Extensions"
.SH NAME
git\-nanny \- clean up dead local git branches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git nanny
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B git nanny restore
.br
.B git nanny \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git\-nanny
lists local branches sorted by how dead they are and deletes the ones you pick.
It finds branches that were merged normally, branches that were merged with a
squash commit, branches whose upstream was deleted on the remote, and branches
nobody has touched for months.
.PP
Squash merges are the reason this tool exists:
.B git branch \-\-merged
does not list them, so the usual one\-liner leaves most of the graveyard behind.
.PP
Run with no scope flag and a terminal attached, git\-nanny opens an interactive
list. Without a terminal, or with a scope flag, it works non\-interactively.
.PP
Every deletion is written to a journal first, so any branch can be restored
afterwards. See
.B JOURNAL
below.
.SH CATEGORIES
Each branch gets exactly one category, which also sets the sort order.
.TP
.B merged
Contained in the default branch, either as an ancestor or through a squash
merge. Preselected in the interactive list.
.TP
.B upstream gone
The branch tracked a remote branch that no longer exists \- usually a merged
pull request. Preselected in the interactive list.
.TP
.B stale
No commits for longer than
.BR \-\-stale\-days ,
and no upstream. Not preselected.
.TP
.B active
Everything else. Not preselected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-merged
Merged branches only.
.TP
.B \-all\-but\-default
Every branch except the default one and the protected ones.
.TP
.B \-yes
Run without asking. Required for any non\-interactive deletion.
.TP
.B \-dry\-run
Only show the plan, delete nothing.
.TP
.B \-force
Also delete branches that have commits the default branch does not.
.TP
.BI \-stale\-days " n"
Days without commits before a branch counts as abandoned. Default 90.
.TP
.BI \-default\-branch " name"
Default branch name. Overrides autodetection.
.TP
.BI \-protect " glob"
Glob of protected branches. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Without
.B \-merged
or
.BR \-all\-but\-default ,
a non\-interactive run deletes nothing: it prints the branch list and asks you
to name a scope. Branches with unique commits are skipped unless
.B \-force
is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B restore
List the branches this tool deleted in the current repository, newest first,
with the commit each one pointed at.
.SH PROTECTION
These branches are never deleted, with or without
.BR \-force :
the current branch, the default branch, any branch checked out in another
worktree, and any branch matching a protection pattern.
.PP
Patterns come from the
.B \-protect
flag and from git config:
.PP
.RS
git config \-\-add nanny.protect 'release/*'
.RE
.PP
A pattern also protects branches below it, so
.I release/*
covers
.IR release/v2/hotfix .
.PP
The default branch is resolved in this order: the
.B nanny.defaultBranch
git config value,
.IR origin/HEAD ,
.IR main ,
.IR master ,
and finally the current branch \- but only when it is the only branch in the
repository. If none of these resolve, git\-nanny refuses to delete anything and
tells you how to name the default branch explicitly.
.SH JOURNAL
Before each deletion a line is appended to
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/git\-nanny/deleted.jsonl ,
by default
.IR ~/.local/state/git\-nanny/deleted.jsonl ,
recording the repository, the branch, the commit and the time. If that write
fails, the branch is not deleted: an unrecorded deletion cannot be undone.
.PP
The journal is keyed on the repository root, so
.B git nanny restore
finds the same records from any subdirectory. Deleted commits stay in the
object database until git collects garbage, which is at least two weeks by
default.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive list:
.PP
.RS
git nanny
.RE
.PP
Delete merged branches, including squash\-merged ones:
.PP
.RS
git nanny \-\-merged \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
Delete everything except the default branch:
.PP
.RS
git nanny \-\-all\-but\-default \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
See what would happen, and what was deleted before:
.PP
.RS
git nanny \-\-dry\-run
.br
git nanny restore
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/git\-nanny/deleted.jsonl
Journal of deleted branches. Honours
.BR XDG_STATE_HOME .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or nothing to do.
.TP
.B 1
At least one branch could not be deleted or journaled, or the default branch
could not be determined.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown subcommand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-branch (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
.SH BUGS
Report at https://github.com/art\-ps/git\-nanny/issues
.SH AUTHOR
Artem Pisarev
